# The repository stores LF, always.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Committing from a shell where core.autocrlf is off turns
# a five-line edit into a whole-file diff, because the index then keeps the CRLF
# the working tree happened to have. That is what happened to README.md in
# 821f00e and to four lib files in 3c48e93: the edit was small, the diff was not,
# and the next reader sees a rewrite where nothing was rewritten. `text=auto`
# makes the normalisation a property of the repository rather than of whoever's
# git config is in effect.
* text=auto